A carve that keeps no bit is not refused: no bits come out as the block of every bit,
so the carve may signal bits its source may not, where it should refuse;
a notification's capability may signal no bit its source may not.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: slot is not derived from its parent
Witness: fuzz notify-carve-bits

diff --git a/kernel/object.h b/kernel/object.h
--- a/kernel/object.h
+++ b/kernel/object.h
@@ -380,7 +380,7 @@ static inline bool notify_block(uint32_t bits, uint32_t *code)
 {
     uint32_t low = bits & (0u - bits);
     uint32_t end = bits + low;          /* the bit past the block, 0 when the block reaches bit 31 */
-    if (bits == 0 || (end & (end - 1)) != 0) {
+    if ((end & (end - 1)) != 0) {
         return false;
     }
     uint32_t first = pow2_log(low);
